d implementing new fraud  fighting tools the director says they  know many are falling victim to fraud  especially with the bank of america  debit cards  she says every day they send claims to  the bank to be reinstated  but the bank is now behind we are  working on  resolving that um and my understanding  right now is that bank of america does  have a backlog  in terms of unfreezing cards joe mohler  8 news now  several state lawmakers say modernizing  the computers and software at dieter  this  session is a priority right now there  are four separate bill draft requests  addressing  unemployment in the system here in  nevada coming up next on politics now  will helping the climate hurt jobs  alexander limon will join us to break  down the executive orders  signed by the biden administration this  week you're watching  politics now  [Music]  energy secretary nominee jennifer  granholm says the administration the  biden administration  will focus on green jobs she also told  the senate energy and natural resources  committee that  she opposes using yucca mountain to  store nuclear waste  nevada senator catherine cortez masto  sits on that  committee granholm is the former  governor of michigan  the byte administration says it will  take decisive and immediate action to  combat climate change  the president announced several  executive orders to clean energy and  lower emissions  the bite administration's plan will also  focus on low-income communities across  the country  where high emissions increase asthma and  cancer rates  it creates both a white house  interagency  task force to address environmental  justice  as well as an advisory council it  directs the department of health and  human services to create an  office of climate change and health  equity  the biden team says it will offset job  losses in the oil and gas industry  by transitioning the workforce to the  clean energy sector  our washington dc correspondent  alexander limon joining us now to talk  a