der  week every single day president biden  came out and signed executive orders on  one topic or another so  a racial equality that was one day and  he directed this was a big one he  brought  the justice department to phase out and  end contracts with  private for-profit prisons because we  know that the prison system  and especially the for-profit prison  system negatively  impacts and disproportionately impacts  communities of color  um so that was one thing he also  directed the department of housing and  urban development  to try to deal with some of these  historic and systemic issues that we see  that prevent black and  hispanic and other minority communities  from buying their first home and  you know and president biden talked  about you know that prevents them from  building equity and ever being able to  build  generational wealth like we see you know  white counterparts do  and that was alexander limon reporting  from washington dc  coming up next on politics now nevada  doesn't have a lottery  why is that you're watching politics now  [Music]  well there were long lines for powerball  and mega millions jackpots across the  country but  not here in nevada so why doesn't nevada  have  the lottery we certainly have plenty of  other gambling well it was actually  outlawed in the original nevada state  constitution passed in 1864  and since then plenty of bills to remove  that language have been written but  they've all died a very quick  death the closest attempt was in 2009  it was passed by the state assembly but  it failed in the senate  since it's in the constitution this kind  of measure would have to pass  both houses in carson city in two  consecutive sessions  and then get approved in a general  election ballot  it was done through an initiative  petition that would need to go on two  straight  general election ballots essentially  it's a long road  here's a look at what to watch as we  mentioned earlier the 2021 legislative  session starts in cars